# git-annex routing for a legal-text preservation dataset.
#
# The DataLad default (annex only what is binary) is WRONG here: every
# preserved byte in raw/ is text -- JSON, XHTML, XML -- and getting that text
# out of git history is the entire reason this is an annexed dataset rather
# than a plain repository. So raw/ is routed explicitly, by path, not by
# mimeencoding.
#
# Conversely index/ and raw/source-catalog.edn must stay in git proper. They
# are what a consumer reads to query the corpus and to verify custody of it;
# if they were annexed, answering "which acts amend this one?" would require
# downloading gigabytes first.
#
# Later lines win, so the general rule comes first and the exceptions after.

* annex.backend=SHA256E
* annex.largefiles=((mimeencoding=binary)and(largerthan=0))

**/.git* annex.largefiles=nothing
README.md annex.largefiles=nothing
bin/** annex.largefiles=nothing
index/** annex.largefiles=nothing

raw/** annex.largefiles=anything
raw/source-catalog.edn annex.largefiles=nothing
